🔁 WEEK-9 | DAY-7: GRU (Gated Recurrent Unit) Networks

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 What is GRU?

**GRU (Gated Recurrent Unit)** is an advanced version of **RNN**, similar to LSTM but:

👉 Simpler
👉 Faster
👉 Efficient

It is designed to:

✔ Capture long-term dependencies
✔ Solve vanishing gradient problem

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Why GRU?

Basic RNN:

❌ Cannot handle long sequences

LSTM:

✔ Powerful but complex

GRU:

✔ Simpler than LSTM
✔ Comparable performance
✔ Faster training

---

🧠 Key Idea

GRU uses **gates** to control information flow, but fewer gates than LSTM.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔑 GRU Components (Gates)

GRU has only **2 gates**:

---

1️⃣ Update Gate (zₜ)

Controls how much past information to keep.

[
z_t = \sigma(W_z [h_{t-1}, x_t])
]

---

2️⃣ Reset Gate (rₜ)

Controls how much past information to forget.

[
r_t = \sigma(W_r [h_{t-1}, x_t])
]

---

3️⃣ Candidate Hidden State

[
\tilde{h}*t = tanh(W [r_t \cdot h*{t-1}, x_t])
]

---

4️⃣ Final Hidden State

[
h_t = (1 - z_t) \cdot h_{t-1} + z_t \cdot \tilde{h}_t
]

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 GRU Architecture

```text id="gru1"
Input → Reset Gate → Update Gate → Hidden State → Output
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔥 Why GRU is Efficient

✔ Fewer parameters than LSTM
✔ Faster training
✔ Less memory usage

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 GRU vs LSTM vs RNN

| Feature     | RNN        | LSTM      | GRU       |
| ----------- | ---------- | --------- | --------- |
| Memory      | Short-term | Long-term | Long-term |
| Gates       | None       | 3 gates   | 2 gates   |
| Complexity  | Low        | High      | Medium    |
| Speed       | Fast       | Slow      | Faster    |
| Performance | Low        | High      | High      |

